On Mar 1, 2014, at 6:18 PM, Aki Vehtari <Aki.V...@aalto.fi> wrote:

> ...
> Would it be possible to have a block in Stan language for computations over
> samples? Block called, for example, "summary quantities"?

I really wish there was an easy way to do this.  I'm open to suggestions
anyone might have on how we could do it.

As is, we stream out the samples to file in CmdStan, and write them to memory
in RStan and PyStan.  And we calculate each chain independently (in its own
process) in CmdStan (and sometimes in RStan depending on the call).

We'd need some way to aggregate samples in memory then give access to functions.
I'm thinking something like the extract() function in RStan would be nice that
gives you, for instance you get the draws for matrix parameter m as
m[chain,draw,row,col] or m[draw,row,col] if you've aggregated chains.  And
then the aggregation by default scrambles them, but you can also get them
unscrambled.

- Bob

