That's why I included the transform example that returns the transformed
parameter and increments the log probability with the Jacobian adjustment.
Then you could write:

  transform(x,...) ~ ...;

instead of

  increment_log_prob(log_jacobian_transform(x,...));
  transform(x,...) ~ ...

Right now, that would be useful in cases of vectors with varying
lower and upper bound constraints, which we don't currently support.

