We do split out what we need from Boost and Eigen for RStan to
reduce size.  But Boost likes to include other packages, so it's
a big tangle.  And we only need a bit of each package we use.

We left everything in for the regular distribution
because we tend to develop from there and are continually bringing
in new pieces.

We don't really have any dependencies on particular versions
of Boost or Eigen.   The main problem with supporting multiple versions is
that we don't have the testing compute power or person power to
run all the combinatorics.

- Bob

