There is a unit_vector type in Stan right now which uses spherical coordinates.  For posteriors which are strongly multimodal or broadly dispersed on the sphere the parameterization that this is using may cause problems with adaptation due to the infinite sum issue Michael mentioned.  For more peaked distributions it should work fine in practice.  (Modes narrower than pi or pi/2 should be fine...)

I have a half finished paper looking at evaluating other ways to parameterize the sphere for MCMC...I should really get back to it.

