The driving factor will be Michael's re-do of auto-diff, and I
don't think that's going to be ready to merge into Stan for a while.

If we go to C++11 in the code, we're going to need to use C++11 = true
always, not just by default.  Before that, we need to make sure C++11
will run everywhere we need it to.

I can't keep track of all these Windows compilers --- is mingw-g++-4.6
what's distributed with Rtools?  I can't make heads or tails of this
page:

   http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/

It'd be nice if they said which tools were included :-)  And why in
the world don't they freeze a version for the latest release of R?  This
is more helpful:

   http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/Rtools.txt

Our life would be so much easier without supporting either Windows or R
(of course, then we'd lose most of our users, though I guess that'd make
support easier, too :-)).

- Bob

