Some of the BUGS models don't converge with NUTS or Gibbs sampling either, but most do. MCMCpack has random-walk Metropolis that by default uses the MLEs plus a diagonal matrix of scaling parameters to jump.

I don't recall anyone on stan-users wanting to compare Metropolis-Hastings to NUTS, usually it is BUGS to NUTS. I did a few comparisons for my class, and you get pictures like this:

https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-dev/_SJBiCaUbt4/MblkpLElI4MJ

Ben

